.\" wdm(1) -- Wayland display manager that is its own compositor
.\" Written for wdm 0.2.0. Section 1 rather than 8 because wdm.service's
.\" Documentation= already points at man:wdm(1).
.TH WDM 1 "2026-08-03" "wdm 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wdm \- Wayland display manager that is its own compositor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wdm
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-backend
.IR NAME ]
.br
.B wdm
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.RB [ \-V | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wdm
is a display manager for Wayland that is itself the compositor. Every other
Wayland display manager spawns a separate kiosk compositor \(en cage,
weston\-kiosk, gamescope \(en purely to host the greeter window.
.B wdm
binds DRM/KMS directly through libseat, hosts the greeter as an ordinary
Wayland client, and hands the display to the user's session at login. There is
no nesting and no X server.
.PP
The greeter is a separate, unprivileged process. It speaks
.BR wdm_greeter_v1 ,
a Wayland protocol, and never sees the shadow database:
.B wdm
runs PAM itself and forwards each question the stack asks. Three greeters are
available \(en a software\-rendered reference greeter, a GTK4 greeter, and a
WebKitGTK greeter themed in HTML and CSS \(en and any Wayland client that
implements the protocol may replace them.
.PP
At login
.B wdm
does not fork a child compositor. It drops everything holding the display \(en
the DRM device, the renderer, libinput, and the libseat session \(en and only
then execs the user's session, which acquires real DRM master on the same VT.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Read configuration from
.IR PATH .
Default:
.IR /etc/wdm/wdm.toml .
A missing file is not an error and the built\-in defaults are used; a malformed
one is fatal, because continuing would silently ignore a deliberate choice of
VT or greeter.
.TP
.BI \-\-backend " NAME"
Either
.B udev
(real hardware: DRM/KMS, libinput, libseat) or
.B winit
(nested inside an existing Wayland session, as a window).
.B drm
and
.B nested
are accepted as aliases for
.B udev
and
.B winit
respectively. Defaults to
.B udev
when running as root and
.B winit
otherwise. The
.B winit
backend is for development: it cannot exercise DRM, the seat, VT switching, or
the handoff to a session.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file is TOML. Unknown keys are rejected rather than ignored,
so a typo is reported instead of silently doing nothing.
.SS Top level
.TP
.B vt
Virtual terminal to run on. Default:
.BR 7 ,
which is free on a default systemd install \(en
.B getty@tty1.service
is the unit enabled by default and logind autospawns a getty on tty2 through
tty6 on demand. Running there means
.B wdm
needs no
.B Conflicts=
against a getty, and tty1 remains a working text console, which is the recovery
path when a greeter wedges. Must be at least 1.
.IP
.B wdm.service
ships no
.B Conflicts=
because of that default. Setting
.B vt
to a terminal a getty uses \(en 1 through 6 \(en requires a drop-in adding
.BI Conflicts=getty@tty N .service
and
.BI After=getty@tty N .service
for that
.IR N ,
or
.B wdm
and the getty contend for the same VT with nothing arbitrating between them,
and the recovery console documented above is gone.
.TP
.B default_session
Session id offered to a user with no recorded last session.
.B wdm
never preselects a session itself; this is advertised to the greeter as a
fallback, and acting on it is the greeter's policy.
.SS [greeter]
.TP
.B command
Command line for the greeter, split on whitespace and executed directly.
.B It is not run through a shell,
so a configuration file cannot inject shell into a root process. Default:
.IR /usr/lib/wdm/wdm-greeter .
.TP
.B user
Unprivileged account the greeter runs as. Default:
.BR wdm .
Must not be
.BR root :
the greeter is untrusted code hosted by the process that owns DRM master, and
running it as root defeats the privilege split entirely.
.SS [keyboard]
xkb configuration for the login screen. It has to be set here because there is
no user whose preferences could be consulted yet, and someone who cannot type
their password on their own layout cannot log in.
.TP
.B layout
xkb layout. Default:
.BR us .
An empty string is not equivalent \(en xkb would fall back to its own build\-time
default, which need not be
.BR us .
.TP
.BR rules ", " model ", " variant ", " options
The remaining xkb fields, empty by default. For example
.B options
=
.IR ctrl:nocaps .
.SS [[output]]
An array of tables, one per connector, in
.B priority order.
Array position is the rank: the first entry is rank 0, the primary, and that is
where a greeter puts its login form. Connectors not listed rank after every
listed one, sorted by name, so the primary does not move between boots. Ranks
are recomputed on hotplug, so unplugging the primary promotes the next entry.
.TP
.B connector
Connector name as the kernel reports it, for example
.I DP-1
or
.IR eDP-1 .
Required. Listing the same connector twice is an error.
.TP
.B mode
.IR WIDTH x HEIGHT
or
.IR WIDTH x HEIGHT @ REFRESH .
Defaults to the connector's preferred mode.
.TP
.B scale
Output scale. Fractional values are permitted. Must be positive.
.TP
.B transform
One of
.BR normal ", " 90 ", " 180 ", " 270 ", " flipped ", " flipped-90 ", "
.BR flipped-180 ", " flipped-270 .
Default:
.BR normal .
.TP
.B enable
When
.BR false ,
the output is left unprogrammed and given no rank, so no password prompt can
appear on it. It is not actively blanked: whatever was on it before
.B wdm
started remains until the mode times out. Default:
.BR true .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WDM_LOG
Log filter, in the syntax of the Rust
.B env_logger
crate \(en for example
.BR debug ,
or
.BR wdm::login=debug .
Named
.B WDM_LOG
rather than
.B RUST_LOG
so that a user session's own
.B RUST_LOG
cannot reconfigure the display manager's logging.
.TP
.B WDM_LOG_STYLE
Whether log output is coloured:
.BR auto ", " always ", " never .
.TP
.B WDM_GREETER_LOG
Read by the greeters shipped with
.BR wdm ,
not by
.B wdm
itself.
.PP
.B wdm
clears the environment before executing the greeter, so nothing else is
inherited. To trace a greeter's protocol traffic, point
.B greeter.command
at a wrapper script that exports
.BR WAYLAND_DEBUG=1 .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/wdm/wdm.toml
Configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/pam.d/wdm
PAM stack.
.B Authentication fails until this exists;
an "Authentication failure" on the greeter with no PAM file installed is
expected and is not a bug.
.TP
.I /var/lib/wdm/last-session
Per\-user record of the last session launched, reported to the greeter so it can
preselect one.
.TP
.I /run/wdm
Runtime directory, created root\-owned and mode 0700 by systemd;
.B wdm
hands it to the greeter account only after the socket inside it is bound and
secured. The Wayland socket the greeter connects to lives here, mode 0600 and
owned by the same account; every connection's peer uid is checked against it as
well.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/wdm/
Greeter executables.
.TP
.I /usr/share/wdm/webkit-greeter/themes/
Themes for the WebKitGTK greeter.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Shut down cleanly, having been asked to by
.B SIGTERM
or
.BR SIGINT .
.TP
.B 1
Startup failed \(en no GPU on the seat, an unusable greeter account, a socket
that could not be secured, or a fatal error while running.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line.
.SH NOTES
.B wdm
must run as root. It owns DRM master, reads the shadow database through PAM,
and drops privileges itself when launching the greeter and the user's session.
.PP
The VT is switched to before the seat is opened, because seatd binds a client's
session to whichever VT is foreground at that moment rather than allocating
one. A session registered against a VT that is no longer in front is inactive,
holds no DRM master, and cannot commit a frame.
.PP
Ctrl+Alt+F\fIn\fR is handled by
.B wdm
before the greeter sees it, so a wedged greeter can always be escaped from. The
chord has to be handled rather than left to the kernel: a graphical session puts
the console keyboard in
.BR K_OFF ,
so the kernel no longer translates it. It is intercepted for every state
.B wdm
can be in, including the give-up screen shown after a greeter has failed to
start repeatedly, and if the seat refuses the switch
.B wdm
falls back to
.B VT_ACTIVATE
on
.I /dev/tty0
so the escape hatch does not depend on the session layer being healthy.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR seatd (1),
.BR systemd (1),
.BR pam (8),
.BR loginctl (1)
.PP
Project documentation, including the
.B wdm_greeter_v1
protocol and the greeter and theme APIs:
.UR https://quinnjr.github.io/wdm/
.UE
.SH BUGS
The DRM path has had little exposure to real hardware. Report issues at
.UR https://github.com/quinnjr/wdm/issues
.UE
